  "ind_common" [label="(0,0,0) Common pattern from multiple static PEC reports: diffusion/pH losses cause generally low STF/selectivity in low-concentration electrolytes."];
  "n15" [label="(23,0,0) Currently, STF conversion efficiency for CO₂R/water splitting in conventional devices is low (e.g., 0.08%, 0.43%, 0.63%)."];
  "n22" [label="(43,0,0) Currently, reported PEC devices leveraging flowing seawater (2.3 mM HCO₃⁻) without CO₂ bubbling remain largely unexplored."];
  "n23" [label="(48,0,0) Currently, we demonstrate an understudied regime of molecular flux catalysis in which CO₂(aq) reactants continuously flow to catalysts within boundary layer flow."];
  "rule_static" [label="(0,0,0) If static electrolyte uses diffusion-dominant transport causing pH gradients, acid-base reactions, and local CO₂ depletion, then conventional PEC suffers major transport losses and low STF/selectivity."];
